मण्डलम् नमस्कारः ॥   ॰ नमस्कारः — THE DEMONSTRATION'S OWN SOURCE

॰ THE ANSWER IS ५. `पञ्च` returns ५ and `नमस्कारः` hands it back.
॰
॰ THIS LINE IS READ BY A MACHINE, not only by a person: `pradarshana`'s
॰ demonstration parses `THE ANSWER IS <numeral>` out of every file in this
॰ directory, runs the file, and REFUSES if the two disagree. The other five
॰ sources already carried the sentence in this form; this one stated its answer
॰ only in prose, so the demonstration could not check it. Added 2026-09-06 by
॰ the row that made the demonstration run the directory it makes claims about.

॰ THE SMALLEST SASSEMBLY PROGRAM THAT REACHES THE MACHINE. `tools/demo.sh`
॰ compiles this file with the self-hosted chain — lex, parse, resolve, typecheck,
॰ IR, emit (both twins), assemble, link, load, run — and every stage passes.
॰
॰ IT COMES BACK WITH ०, NOT ५, AND THE DEMO SAYS SO ON ITS OWN LINE. That is the
॰ point of the file: it is written to be as small as a program can be and still
॰ hold a literal and a call, so that what the compiler LOSES is visible with
॰ nothing else in the way. Two things are lost, and the demo measures both rather
॰ than repeating them from a margin:
॰
॰   (a) THE LITERAL — CLOSED 2026-09-04. `५` below parses as a numeral and now
॰       reaches the machine carrying its value. UNTIL THEN the IR builder folded
॰       it to ०: `ir.t1:512` calls `अङ्कमूल्यम्`, whose first guard (`ir.t1:454`)
॰       returned ० for any token whose kind was not `पदविभागॱसङ्ख्याभेद` — and
॰       `lex.t1` never produces that kind, BY DESIGN and by its own margin
॰       (`lex.t1:104`), because one lexer serves T0 and T1 and T0 needs the
॰       operand as a word. The parser had moved to deciding numeral-ness by TEXT
॰       and the guard had not moved with it, so no source could satisfy it and the
॰       correct reader behind it was unreachable. `W-257` made the guard accept
॰       what `व्याकर` accepts; 47bad575 fixed the reader itself, which had computed
॰       the radix, validated the digits and then returned the RADIX.
॰       **This demonstration found that guard**, and the row it named is closed.
॰
॰   (b) ARITHMETIC — CLOSED 2026-09-04 by `W-245`. There is deliberately no
॰       `योगः` in THIS file, which is why it was the only one of the six that
॰       reached the machine while the others could not; the IR builder now lowers
॰       arithmetic, and `spec/demo/योगपर्यन्तम्.t1` sums to ५५ with it. Both (a) and
॰       (b) have landed: `पञ्च` below returns ५ and `नमस्कारः` hands it back, with nothing
॰       in this file changed.
॰
॰ WHY TWO ROUTINES. The first routine declared is the module's entry (research/25
॰ §2.6), so `नमस्कारः` is what the startup object calls. Its body is
॰ `प्रत्यागमनम् पञ्च ।` — a routine's bare name in value position, which is a call
॰ with no arguments (`W-237`, `W-228`'s `संज्ञाभेदकोश`) and not a variable read. So
॰ the image that runs holds a real frame, a real `जल` and a real return, and the
॰ demo can show a call reaching the machine even while no value does.

॰ the entry — calls पञ्च and hands its answer back.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः नमस्कारः ददाति न६४ आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् पञ्च ।
इति

॰ the answer this program would give if (a) above were fixed.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः पञ्च ददाति न६४ आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् ५ ।
इति
